# What NOT to send to the Docker daemon when building.
#
# Docker copies the whole directory into the build context before reading the
# Dockerfile. Unfiltered, that is 9GB here — 7.7GB of it a virtualenv the image
# has no use for, since the image installs its own dependencies from
# pyproject.toml.
#
# Note this file is Docker-specific: `docker build` does NOT fall back to
# .gitignore. `gcloud builds submit` does, which is why the cloud build worked
# while a local one would have crawled.

# Virtual environments — the image builds its own
.venv/
venv/
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]

# Node — the API image contains no JavaScript
node_modules/
web/
scripts/pdf/
.next/

# Source documents and the built index. The container reads its corpus from
# Postgres over the network; the PDFs are never needed at runtime.
papers/
data/
artifacts/
models/
.docling_cache/

# History, caches, docs, results
.git/
.gitignore
.github/
.pytest_cache/
.ruff_cache/
.mypy_cache/
.coverage
htmlcov/
docs/
results/
tests/

# Secrets must never enter a build context: every file in it is readable by
# any build step, and can end up in an image layer.
.env
.env.*
!.env.example

# Editors and OS
.DS_Store
.idea/
.vscode/
*.swp
Screenshot*.png
